      "summaries": {
        "en": "WavLM-Base-Plus is a self-supervised speech model that learns rich representations from raw audio without transcriptions, addressing the challenge of limited labeled speech data. Its key innovation is a masked speech denoising task that predicts masked speech segments while preserving speaker identity, enabling it to capture both content and speaker characteristics. You can use it as a feature extractor for downstream tasks like speech recognition or speaker verification, or fine-tune it on your own speech datasets using Hugging Face's Transformers library.",
        "zh": "WavLM-Base-Plus 是一种自监督语音模型，它直接从原始音频中学习丰富的表示，无需依赖转录文本，解决了标注语音数据稀缺的难题。其核心技术在于掩码语音去噪任务——模型在预测被掩码的语音片段时，同时保持说话人身份不变，从而能同时捕捉语音内容和说话人特征。你可以将其作为特征提取器用于语音识别、说话人验证等下游任务，或通过 Hugging Face 的 Transformers 库在自己的语音数据上进行微调，探索其在多语言或噪声环境下的表现。",
        "es": "WavLM-Base-Plus is a self-supervised speech model that learns rich representations from raw audio without transcriptions, addressing the challenge of limited labeled speech data. Its key innovation is a masked speech denoising task that predicts masked speech segments while preserving speaker identity, enabling it to capture both content and speaker characteristics. You can use it as a feature extractor for downstream tasks like speech recognition or speaker verification, or fine-tune it on your own speech datasets using Hugging Face's Transformers library.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "wavlm-base-plus stands out for transformers, pytorch, and wavlm in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "WavLM-Base-Plus is a self-supervised speech model that learns rich representations from raw audio without transcriptions, addressing the challenge of limited labeled speech data. Its key innovation is a masked speech denoising task that predicts masked speech segments while preserving speaker identity, enabling it to capture both content and speaker characteristics. You can use it as a feature extractor for downstream tasks like speech recognition or speaker verification, or fine-tune it on your own speech datasets using Hugging Face's Transformers library.",
          "how": "Review https://huggingface.co/microsoft/wavlm-base-plus for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
      },
